@_alice_evans Anecdotally true IME - every girlboss type I know (and I know a lot) is either happily married or en route, and they have 1-2 kids or plan to.

That’s what “having it all” means.

The childless spinster archetype is a creature of social failure, not social *success*.

@_alice_evans Two immediate questions. 

1. Is there longitudinal data for this? I.e. are university educated women getting married at lower rates than previously? 

2. Is the narrative strongly skewed due to this demographic of women being more prominent in the commentary class?

@_alice_evans Spread of Internet access creating different separate “status hierarchies” in the same location.

Normally people living in the same community have the same status hierarchies enforced by things like shaming/etc

This is less effective because now people can be part of different
